# implements-port B3: -1 does not fit size_t, so the initializer's edge (row int -> size_t) refuses:
# `go`'s implicit throw `convert` (g = 3), uncaught -- the root receives status 3.  Mutant: the edge
# not emitted -- C converts -1 itself and `go` completes with 7.
fn: go () int
    int: x -1
    size_t: s (x)
    return: 7
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
